{
  "name": "1:8 NACA64A204 wing; Re_MAC=5M; 12% chord",
  "data_origin": "Original user left-wing planform scaled uniformly 1:8 (all lengths /8 and area /64); model MAC=0.578625 m; root/tip chords=0.695/0.125 m. NACA 64A204 from the recorded PDAS source is used at every section with zero twist. Angles refer to the nominal NACA chord/global X; the geometric-LE chord rotation is corrected in XFOIL local alpha. Mach=0.2; model-MAC Reynolds numbers 3e6, 5e6, 8e6; angles 0,1,2 degrees. These Reynolds numbers are not divided by 8. Independent 2D XFOIL strips do not solve 3D sweep flow. Geometry comes from supplied sections; coordinates and reference lengths must already be at wind-tunnel model scale. Eta spans only the supplied Y stations; no unprovided wing root, tip or full planform is inferred. All coordinates are interpreted in metres. Upper/lower curve order must match the section contour order. Angle mapping is explicit in the workflow settings. XFOIL is a 2D section method without crossflow. XFOIL computes its own Cp from geometry; imported Cp is not prescribed to its viscous solver. The undisturbed calculation allows natural transition; the requested trip is not imposed in XFOIL. DUMP supplies integral quantities, not resolved u(y). Low-Mach Hk/theta reconstruction is approximate. Re_k reconstruction uses constant freestream kinematic viscosity; DUMP does not provide nu(y) or wall temperature. Laminar confirmation is predicted by the solver transition model, not established experimentally. Filtered from the saved nine-condition boundary-layer dataset; no solver rerun.",
